  "answer_text": "In *The Vampire Diaries*, Elena's transformation into a vampire is a major turning point in the series. Here's a full breakdown:\n\n---\n\n### \ud83e\udddb When Does Elena Turn Into a Vampire?\n\nElena Gilbert begins her transformation in the **Season 3 finale, Episode 22**, titled **\"The Departed,\"** where she drowns after being in a car accident with Matt Donovan.\n\nThough Dr. Meredith Fell had secretly given Elena vampire blood to heal an earlier injury, this leads to her transformation when she dies.\n\nShe **officially transitions** into a vampire in the **first episode of Season 4**, titled **\"Growing Pains.\"**\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\ude97 How Did It Happen?\n\nRebekah deliberately caused Matt's vehicle to crash, making the car swerve off Wickery Bridge and plunge into the water below. Although a distraught Stefan arrived on time to save them, Elena urged him to save Matt first \u2014 and by the time Stefan pulled Elena out of the water, she had breathed her last.\n\nUnbeknownst to everyone, Elena had vampire blood in her system when she died, as Dr. Meredith Fell had injected it to save her from fatal injuries. The regenerative vampire blood in her bloodstream prevented her from truly dying, causing her to return as a vampire in Season 4, Episode 1, \"Growing Pains.\"\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\ude31 Was It Intentional?\n\nElena became a vampire **despite never wanting to be one.** To complete her transformation, Elena had to ingest human blood, but she tried her utmost to do so without taking a life.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udc8a Does She Stay a Vampire?\n\nElena woke up as a vampire in Season 3, Episode 22, \"The Departed,\" and remained a vampire for all of **Seasons 4, 5, and 6**, only getting cured back into a human at the **end of Season 6**.",
